.TH mnnn-mcp 1  "mnnn-mcp 2.21.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-mcp \- MCP: serve Muninn to MCP clients (stdio or HTTP, named revocable clients with roles), and add external MCP servers whose tools rule sets can call
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn mcp\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-log\-file\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-transport\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
MCP: serve Muninn to MCP clients (stdio or HTTP, named revocable clients with roles), and add external MCP servers whose tools rule sets can call
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Write logs to this file instead of stderr (the TUI defaults to <home>/logs/tui.log)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_LOG_FILE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-transport\fR \fI<stream|poll>\fR
How live collaboration reaches peers: `stream` (gRPC streams, the default) or `poll` (requests over the peer connection; for containers). Overrides MUNINN_COLLAB_TRANSPORT and the `net config \-\-collab\-transport` setting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH NOTES
.PP
Muninn speaks the Model Context Protocol both ways. `mnnn mcp serve` makes it an MCP server (stdio for one named client, or HTTP on 127.0.0.1:4743 with client tokens); nothing is served until you start it. Every caller is a named client with a role: read (the default), write, run or full; revoke one at any time. Writes and runs are recorded in the history with origin mcp. `mnnn mcp add` adds an external MCP server whose tools rule sets can call (`then mcp SERVER TOOL k=v`) and read in conditions (`\-\-if 'mcp:SERVER/TOOL#path > 3'`); its credentials are kept in the encrypted store and never printed. Each tool must be approved before its first call. `mnnn help mcp` has the guide.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-serve(1)
Serve Muninn over MCP: stdio for one client (`\-\-client NAME`), or HTTP (`\-\-http`)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-client(1)
The clients allowed to call this node\*(Aqs MCP server
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-add(1)
Add an external MCP server: `\-\-url URL` (HTTP) or `\-\- COMMAND ARGS…` (stdio)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-list(1)
External MCP servers
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-show(1)
One server: how it is reached, its credential names, approved tools
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-edit(1)
Change a server\*(Aqs credentials (added or replaced by name)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-remove(1)
Remove a server (and its approvals)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-tools(1)
The tools a server offers (asks it now)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-call(1)
Call a tool: `mnnn mcp call SERVER TOOL key=value …` (asks before its first call)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-approve(1)
Allow a tool to be called (rule sets need this before its first call)
.TP
mnnn\-mcp\-unapprove(1)
Withdraw a tool\*(Aqs approval
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
